    "recommendations": "Ensuring the driveway and access road remain clear of obstructions and can accommodate emergency vehicles throughout their full length could significantly improve response times and apparatus positioning at this property. Given the single point of entry and extended driveway, maintaining adequate vertical clearance and surface width along the travel path would support emergency vehicle access to both the main building and detached structure. Clearly marking the primary access point at the street frontage may assist responding personnel in locating the entry during low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Where dense vegetation limits sightlines along the driveway corridor, managing growth within the immediate travel path could enhance responder visibility and navigation. Identifying and communicating any secondary access options to the rear of the property to local emergency services may support more effective operational staging."
