    "recommendations": "Reducing brush and vegetation concentrations in the immediate area surrounding the structure would improve defensible space and reduce direct fuel exposure to the building. Where trees are clustered near the structure or adjacent to one another, increasing horizontal separation between tree canopies and creating vertical separation between ground-level vegetation and lower tree branches may reduce fuel continuity across the property. Managing scattered shrubs and mixed vegetation cover within the near structure zone could further limit the opportunity for fire to carry through continuous fuels toward the building. The vegetated access route should be maintained with adequate width and overhead clearance to support firefighter access and safe evacuation movement. Keeping the access route clear of encroaching vegetation along its edges and overhead canopy would support suppression operations and reduce the potential for the route to become compromised. Ongoing vegetation management within the immediate structure perimeter, given the limited open space currently observed, would support long-term wildfire resilience."
